data.content:
**No Thread.Abort migration is needed here.**

Your code only uses `Thread.Start()`, `Thread.Join()`, and `Thread.Sleep()` — these APIs work identically in .NET 8. There are no calls to `Thread.Abort`, no `ThreadAbortException` catch blocks, no `Thread.ResetAbort`, and no `Thread.Interrupt`. This code will compile and run correctly as-is on .NET 8.

**Optional modernization (unrelated to Thread.Abort):** You could simplify this with `Parallel.ForEach` or `Task.WhenAll`:

```csharp
public async Task RunBatchAsync(List<WorkItem> items)
{
    await Task.WhenAll(items.Select(item => Task.Run(() => Process(item))));
}
```

But this is purely a style/performance improvement — not a Thread.Abort migration concern.
